WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:03.270
Where a wide river squeezes
through a narrow gorge,

2
00:00:03.320 --> 00:00:06.200
the water rushes through much faster.

3
00:00:06.250 --> 00:00:09.260
The same happens wherever a pipe narrows.

4
00:00:09.310 --> 00:00:12.740
A third of the area, three times as fast.

5
00:00:12.790 --> 00:00:16.820
Every second, the same volume
passes through each section.

6
00:00:16.870 --> 00:00:19.120
No water piles up anywhere.

7
00:00:19.170 --> 00:00:23.980
So where the water is fastest, is the
pressure higher or lower than in the wide

8
00:00:24.030 --> 00:00:25.190
part?

9
00:00:25.240 --> 00:00:28.740
In this mission, you'll model
water as an ideal fluid,

10
00:00:28.790 --> 00:00:31.800
and follow the energy
it carries as it flows.

11
00:00:31.850 --> 00:00:34.410
Then you'll pierce the
side of an open tank,

12
00:00:34.460 --> 00:00:37.430
and predict how fast the jet escapes.

13
00:00:37.480 --> 00:00:42.550
Your mission: predict whether the pressure
goes up or down where the pipe narrows,

14
00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:43.810
and explain why.
